ClojureWasm independently reimplements the Clojure language. The namespaces
under src/lang/clj/clojure/** implement Clojure / Clojure-contrib APIs
(originally (c) Rich Hickey and contributors, Eclipse Public License 1.0).

Ten files reproduce upstream source text and retain the original notice
under EPL-2.0 per EPL-1.0 §7:
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/core_meta.clj (docstrings, verbatim from clojure.core)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/core/protocols.clj (docstrings)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/core/reducers.clj (clojure.core.reducers, by Rich Hickey)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/core/specs/alpha.clj (clojure.core.specs.alpha, by Rich Hickey)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/datafy.clj (clojure.datafy, by Rich Hickey)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/spec/alpha.clj (clojure.spec.alpha, by Rich Hickey)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/set.clj (docstrings, from clojure.set by Rich Hickey)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/spec/gen/alpha.clj (clojure.spec.gen.alpha, by Rich Hickey)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/template.clj (clojure.template, by Stuart Sierra)
  - src/lang/clj/clojure/test/junit.clj (clojure.test.junit, by Jason Sankey)

All other namespaces are independent reimplementations (no upstream source
text reproduced). ClojureWasm is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
Clojure project.

The list above is checked against the tree by scripts/check_clj_attribution.sh:
a file carrying the upstream copyright banner must appear here, and a file
listed here must carry it. It read "Three files" while six more had grown the
banner, which is why it is gated now rather than maintained by hand.
